  "net_asymmetry_caveat": "NET FOLD ASYMMETRY: tier1/v29 select on M/2 worlds and are priced on the disjoint M/2; the net's pick is world-independent, so its two folds agree and its arb is a FULL-M difference \u2014 same estimand, LESS noise. Its winner's-curse control is the ROOT split, not the world split. Do not read a net-vs-rollout gap of order the noise as a strength difference.",
